   "date": "2015-09-24T04:54:28Z",
   "subject": "Totally new to lavaan and R… trying to run CFA...",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I am trying to run a CFA. I have defined my model and that seems to go ok. I then do the model fit and that seems to work. However, when I then use the summary() function the output reads:</div><div><br></div><div><div>Length     Class      Mode </div><div>        1 character character </div></div><div><br></div><div>This seems to be telling me that my model is a categorical variable, right? Am I using incorrect syntax? Why might this be occurring and what is the correct syntax to be using?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for your help.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tEgYM0pMBQAJ",
   "from": "yrosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2015-09-24T06:18:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: Totally new to lavaan and R… trying to run CFA...",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 09/24/2015 06:54 AM, Sgars wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I am trying to run a CFA. I have defined my model and that seems to go\r<br>&gt; ok. I then do the model fit and that seems to work. However, when I then\r<br>&gt; use the summary() function the output reads:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Length     Class      Mode\r<br>&gt;          1 character character\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Make sure that the first argument of the summary() function is your \r<br>fitted lavaan object (often called &#39;fit&#39;), as in:\r<br>\r<br>HS.model &lt;- &#39;\r<br>     visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\r<br>     textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\r<br>     speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9\r<br>&#39;\r<br>\r<br>fit &lt;- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939)\r<br>summary(fit)\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>It would seem to me that you have typed\r<br>\r<br>summary(HS.model)\r<br>\r<br>(or something similar), which would give you the output you got.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
