   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 06/25/2017 09:32 AM, Mahima Raina wrote:\r<br>&gt; Also , please see this\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Attaching package: ‘sem’ The following objects are masked from \r<br>&gt; ‘package:lavaan’: cfa, sem\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Is this relevant ?\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Yes, very much so. It means that you have loaded another package (sem), \r<br>which overwrites the lavaan functions cfa/sem.\r<br>\r<br>Either do not load the sem package (at least not in the same R session \r<br>as you are using lavaan), or use the lavaan:: prefix to call lavaan&#39;s \r<br>cfa() function, as in\r<br>\r<br>fit &lt;- lavaan::cfa(model1,data=mydata1)\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
