     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>That function will choose the correct summary method based on the type of object you give it.  If you don&#39;t load the sem package (only load the lavaan package), then you won&#39;t encounter an issue.  Here is a tutorial on lavaan you can read:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427059185000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wwuvcrDT-6_WByrtFbxS2\">lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/index.html</a><br></div></div>"
